#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Welcome to *Fundamentals of Quantum Algorithms,* the second course in the *Understanding Quantum Information and Computation* series comprising the following courses:\n"
msgstr "Bine ai venit la *Fundamentals of Quantum Algorithms,* al doilea curs din seria *Understanding Quantum Information and Computation*, care cuprinde următoarele cursuri:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Basics of quantum information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information)\n"
msgstr "[Basics of quantum information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fundamentals of quantum algorithms (this course)\n"
msgstr "Fundamentals of quantum algorithms (acest curs)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[General formulation of quantum information](/learning/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information)\n"
msgstr "[General formulation of quantum information](/learning/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Foundations of quantum error correction](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction)\n"
msgstr "[Foundations of quantum error correction](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This course explores computational advantages of quantum information, including what we can do with quantum computers and their advantages over classical computers.\n"
"It begins with quantum query algorithms, which offer simple proof-of-concept demonstrations for quantum algorithms, and then moves on to quantum algorithms for problems\n"
"including integer factorization and unstructured search.\n"
msgstr ""
"Acest curs explorează avantajele computaționale ale informației cuantice, inclusiv ce putem face cu calculatoarele cuantice și avantajele lor față de calculatoarele clasice.\n"
"Începe cu algoritmii de interogare cuantică, care oferă demonstrații simple de tip proof-of-concept pentru algoritmii cuantici, și continuă cu algoritmi cuantici pentru probleme\n"
"precum factorizarea numerelor întregi și căutarea nestructurată.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This course is intended for students, professionals, and hobbyists in fields such as computer science, physics, engineering, and mathematics who are eager to gain knowledge on the theoretical foundations of quantum information and computation.\n"
msgstr "Acest curs este destinat studenților, profesioniștilor și pasionaților din domenii precum informatica, fizica, ingineria și matematica, care doresc să dobândească cunoștințe despre bazele teoretice ale informației și computației cuantice.\n"

